1
00:00:00,099 --> 00:00:01,809
(Q11（单选）) Good evening, everyone.

2
00:00:01,809 --> 00:00:11,169
Let me start by welcoming you all to this talk and thanking you for taking the time to consider joining ACE voluntary organisation.

3
00:00:11,169 --> 00:00:20,669
ACE offers support to people and services in the local area and we’re now looking for more volunteers to help us do this. ACE

4
00:00:20,669 --> 00:00:32,318
[Q11答案句（C）： squashed = close    + Q11干扰项B（bring in 拿来，带来，不是借来，所以不能说明not enough）] By the way, I hope you’re all comfortable – we have brought in extra seats so that no one has to stand, but it does mean that the people at the back of the room may be a bit squashed.

5
00:00:32,318 --> 00:00:37,312
We’ll only be here for about half an hour so, hopefully, that’s OK.

6
00:00:37,312 --> 00:00:44,014
(Q12) One of the first questions we’re often asked is how old you need to be to volunteer.

7
00:00:44,014 --> 00:00:53,615
Well, you can be as young as 16 or you can be 60 or over; it all depends on what type of voluntary work you want to do.

8
00:00:53,615 --> 00:01:03,680
[Q12答案句A ： age isn't relate to ... = less important.  + Q12干扰项B排除，说明reliability很重要] Other considerations, such as reliability, are crucial in voluntary work and age isn’t related to these, in our experience.

9
00:01:03,680 --> 00:01:07,751
(Q13) Another question we get asked relates to training.

10
00:01:07,751 --> 00:01:12,487
[Q13干扰项C online 反义词] Well, there’s plenty of that and it’s all face-to-face.

11
00:01:12,487 --> 00:01:21,963
[Q13答案句（A） = continuous] What’s more, training doesn’t end when you start working for us – it takes place before, during and after periods of work.

12
00:01:21,963 --> 00:01:29,326
[Q13干扰项B： 不由manager进行] Often, it’s run by other experienced volunteers as managers tend to prefer to get on with other things.

13
00:01:29,326 --> 00:01:37,299
(Q14&15（多选）) Now, I would ask you to consider a couple of important issues before you decide to apply for voluntary work.

14
00:01:37,299 --> 00:01:49,959
[Q13干扰项， 排除C work experience] We don’t worry about why you want to be a volunteer – people have many different reasons that range from getting work experience to just doing something they’ve always wanted to do.

15
00:01:49,959 --> 00:02:03,106
[Q13答案句E： enough hours = availability] But it is critical that you have enough hours in the day for whatever role we agree is suitable for you – if being a volunteer becomes stressful then it’s best not to do it at all.

16
00:02:03,106 --> 00:02:08,423
[干扰项A 排除： but we don't ask x x x] You may think that your income is important, but we don’t ask about that.

17
00:02:08,423 --> 00:02:12,533
It’s up to you to decide if you can work without earning money.

18
00:02:12,533 --> 00:02:15,580
[Q14答案句B： level of commitment] What we value is dedication.

19
00:02:15,580 --> 00:02:24,346
Some of our most loyal volunteers earn very little themselves but still give their full energy to the work they do with us.

20
00:02:24,346 --> 00:02:33,290
(Q16（Matching）) [筹款与垃圾清理] OK, so let’s take a look at some of the work areas that we need volunteers for and the sort of things that would help you in those.

21
00:02:33,290 --> 00:02:36,887
You may wish simply to help us raise money.

22
00:02:36,887 --> 00:02:51,015
If you have the creativity to come up with an imaginative or novel way of fundraising, we’d be delighted, as standing in the local streets or shops with a collection box can be rather boring!

23
00:02:51,015 --> 00:03:03,447
One outdoor activity that we need volunteers for is litter collection and for this it’s useful if you can walk for long periods, sometimes uphill.

24
00:03:03,447 --> 00:03:11,320
Some of our regular collectors are quite elderly, but very active and keen to protect the environment.

25
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:17,987
[儿童健康活动与故事俱乐部] If you enjoy working with children, we have three vacancies for what are called ‘playmates’.

26
00:03:17,987 --> 00:03:25,357
These volunteers help children learn about staying healthy through a range of out-of-school activities.

27
00:03:25,357 --> 00:03:34,448
You don’t need to have children yourself, but it’s good if you know something about nutrition and can give clear instructions.

28
00:03:34,448 --> 00:03:45,696
If that doesn’t appeal to you, maybe you would be interested in helping out at our story club for disabled children, especially if you have done some acting.

29
00:03:45,696 --> 00:03:55,296
We put on three performances a year based on books they have read and we’re always looking for support with the theatrical side of this.

30
00:03:55,296 --> 00:04:07,036
[急救服务与初期学习] The last area I’ll mention today is first aid. Volunteers who join this group can end up teaching others in vulnerable groups who may be at risk of injury.

31
00:04:07,036 --> 00:04:16,036
Initially, though, your priority will be to take in a lot of information and not forget any important steps or details.

32
00:04:16,036 --> 00:04:18,536
Right, so does anyone have any questions …

